Old and New Vol 1 Clifton Hall Stairway 0158.jpg","year":1900,"author":"Charles Latham (1847-1912)","licence":"Public domain"}],"article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manor_of_Clifton","cat":"Clifton Hall, Nottinghamshire","stories":[{"layer":"clifton","text":"The Clifton family held the manor of Clifton from the late 13th century, and this was their manor house.[^s1] Sir Gervase Clifton largely rebuilt it between 1778 and 1797, partly to designs by John Carr of York.[^s1] In 1958 the family sold it, ending 700 years of ownership; it became a girls' grammar school, and is now two houses.[^s1] The hall itself dates from the late 16th century and is listed Grade I. In its grounds are a brick ice house of the mid-18th century, the vaulted remains of a curved garden stairway, a pair of Coade stone lions of the early 19th century, and the late 18th-century stable block, now cottages.[^s2]","source":{"title":"Manor of Clifton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manor_of_Clifton","kind":"Wikipedia"},"sources":[{"title":"Listed buildings in Nottingham (Clifton South ward)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Listed_buildings_in_Nottingham_(Clifton_South_ward)","kind":"Wikipedia"}],"cites":{"s1":{"title":"Manor of Clifton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manor_of_Clifton","kind":"Wikipedia"},"s2":{"title":"Listed buildings in Nottingham (Clifton South ward)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Listed_buildings_in_Nottingham_(Clifton_South_ward)","kind":"Wikipedia"}},"when":"13th century","whenSrc":{"title":"Manor of Clifton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manor_of_Clifton","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"Clifton Hall","see":[["Sir Robert Clifton's colliery","69731"],["Clifton estate","p723"]]}],"sum":"The Manor of Clifton was a historic manor situated near the City of Nottingham, England. The manor house, known as Clifton Hall is situated on the right bank of the River Trent in the village of Clifton, Nottinghamshire,. about 3+1⁄2 miles south-west of the historic 